# AI/LLM conventions

Authoritative references:
[`ai-and-llm.md`](mdc:docs/plans/architecture/ai-and-llm.md) — end-to-end map of where LLM is used.
[`llm-provider-layer.md`](mdc:docs/plans/architecture/llm-provider-layer.md) — transport layer (providers, routing, key save).

## Non-negotiables

- **All LLM calls go through `LLMManager`.** Get the singleton via
  `from services.ai import get_llm_manager`. Never instantiate a
  provider class (`OpenAIProvider`, `AnthropicProvider`, …) directly.
- **Every call gates on the master switches.**
  - `AppSettings.ai_enabled` (master kill switch).
  - The relevant per-feature flag (`ai_resolution_analysis`,
    `ai_opportunity_scoring`, `ai_news_sentiment`, `news_workflow_*`,
    `cortex_enabled`, …). If your code has a new use-case, add a
    feature flag — don't piggy-back on an unrelated one.
- **Budget-aware code paths use `CycleBudget`.** The news pipeline's
  `services/news/workflow_orchestrator.py:CycleBudget` enforces
  per-cycle / per-hour / monthly caps. New batch consumers either use
  it or implement an equivalent pre-call check against
  `LLMUsageLog` running totals — never call into the LLM in an
  unbounded loop.
- **`LLMUsageLog.purpose` is mandatory.** Pass a stable purpose
  string (`"opportunity_judge"`, `"resolution_analysis"`,
  `"news_workflow:edge_estimation"`, `"cortex_agent"`, …). The AI
  Activity tab and `/sync-docs` rely on it.
- **Model selection.** Default = `AppSettings.ai_default_model`.
  Premium = `ai_premium_model` (opt-in only — never escalate
  silently). Per-purpose overrides via
  `AppSettings.llm_model_assignments` (JSON map).
- **`structured_output(...)` over free-form `chat(...)` for any
  decision-driving call.** Define an explicit JSON schema; do not
  parse free text.
- **Track the LLM-vs-classical-ML split.** semantic matching
  (FAISS + sentence-transformers), entity-overlap NER, Cox-PH fill
  model, article clustering — these are NOT LLM. Don't replace them
  with LLM calls "to be consistent."

## Common footguns this rule exists to prevent

- Hard-coding a model id (`"gpt-4o"`) inside a service. Use
  `manager.default_model` or read `llm_model_assignments[purpose]`.
- Silent fallback to default model when a per-purpose model is
  configured but the provider is missing — log and surface the
  misconfiguration instead.
- Adding an LLM call inside a tight strategy loop without a budget
  gate — exhausts `ai_max_monthly_spend` invisibly.
- Using `LLMManager` outside `services/ai/`, `services/news/`,
  `services/strategy_reverse_engineer/`, `services/autoresearch_service.py`,
  or routes that proxy to them. Strategies in `services/strategies/`
  reach LLM only via the news pipeline / opportunity_judge / verifier
  hooks documented in `ai-and-llm.md`.

